# Crash Detector — the Docker build context, restricted at its source.
#
# AUTHORITY: created under CD-D-013 (BL-20260819T052900Z-0007), which added exactly this
# one path to CD-DISPATCH-WO2-ENGINEER writable_scope. The seat stopped and escalated
# CD-ENG-F25 rather than creating it on its own initiative, and this file exists because
# the Project Lead ruled on it, not because it was obviously needed.
#
# WHY IT IS DESIGN AND NOT BUILD (RT-B remains FORBIDDEN in WO-2). This file declares what
# the context EXCLUDES. It builds nothing, starts nothing and pulls nothing. It sits inside
# deliverable A6, "the container set as DESIGN".
#
# WHY IT MATTERS. deploy/compose.yaml sets every service's build context to `..` — the
# repository root — because the Dockerfiles copy `src/` and `deploy/entrypoints/`. Without
# this file, `docker build` uploads the ENTIRE repository to the daemon: the git history,
# the whole governance record, the pinned PBG framework, the planted violations, and any
# .env or key material that ever lands in the tree. Two distinct harms, and the first is
# the one people forget:
#
#   1  THE CONTEXT ITSELF. Everything sent to the daemon is readable by the daemon and by
#      anything that can talk to it, whether or not a COPY ever names it.
#   2  THE LAYERS. A `COPY . .` in any future Dockerfile — or a `COPY src/` that somebody
#      widens — bakes whatever is in the context into an image layer, where deleting it in
#      a later layer does not remove it.
#
# THE RULE THIS FILE FOLLOWS: exclude by DEFAULT nothing the build needs, and never let the
# governance record or the framework near the daemon. What the build needs is exactly
# `src/`, `deploy/entrypoints/`, `contracts/`, and the dependency manifests.
#
# Checked by tools/register/check_dockerignore.py, which resolves each required exclusion
# against the pattern set rather than looking for a line of text — `.git`, `.git/` and
# `**/.git` all satisfy the requirement, and the check judges the effect.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Version control. Carries every version of every file ever committed, including any that
# were removed. The single largest and least obvious leak in a naive build context.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# THE GOVERNANCE RECORD AND THE PINNED FRAMEWORK. Neither is application code and neither
# belongs in an image. `pbg/` is a read-only snapshot this seat may not modify at all
# (PBG-FWK-013); `governance/` carries authority records, dispatches, decisions and the
# Build Log. A container has no use for either, and an attacker with a shell in a container
# should not be handed the project's own map of its controls.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
governance
pbg
pbg-manifest.yaml
docs
PID.md
BLUEPRINT.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# THE PLANTED VIOLATIONS. plants/ holds deliberate breaches of the doctrine-bearing
# criteria as applyable patches. They are audit instruments and they must never be inside
# a runnable image — a container carrying a patch that adds a numeric default is carrying
# the defect in a form somebody could apply.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
plants

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Secrets, by class rather than by name. Nothing matching these should ever exist in this
# tree — secrets are referenced by env-var NAME only (PBG-SEC-002, non-waivable) — and that
# is exactly why the exclusion is here: this is the layer that holds when the convention
# does not. `.env*` covers .env, .env.local, .env.production and anything else in the family.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
.env
.env*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*_rsa
*_ed25519
secrets
.netrc
.pgpass

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Build and test residue. Compiled bytecode from the HOST interpreter is not the bytecode
# the image's interpreter would produce, and shipping it means shipping a stale cache that
# can shadow the source it was compiled from.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.eggs
build
dist
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.tox
.coverage
htmlcov
.hypothesis

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Environments and editor noise. A .venv is host-specific binaries; copying one into an
# image is how a wheel built for the host's libc ends up in a container that cannot run it.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
.venv
venv
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.swp

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The register checks and the test suite. Audit instruments, not runtime code. Excluded so
# the image contains what it runs and nothing else — the smaller the image, the shorter the
# list of things that have to be true about it.
#
# NOTE FOR WHOEVER BUILDS AT WO-3: if a future service is meant to run a register check
# inside a container, this exclusion is the line to revisit, deliberately and with a
# reason. It is not here by accident.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
tools
tests
required-tests.yaml
